
  ! job "stuck" declares stop, so its cmd is a launcher wtm waits on until it exits (like `docker compose up -d`) — if it keeps running, drop stop to run it in the foreground


  ✗ Jobs that change foreign data — data this worktree does not own:
    migrate changes db — its source's data: this worktree is verbatim
    pass --force to run them anyway, or give this worktree its own data: wtm env <branch> --isolation isolated

